========================================================================
SOURCE (7.10 parse-env — live after Domain A)
========================================================================

```
pub fn c_parse_secret_env(src: String) -> String
  needle = "// " + "SECRET:"          // one prefix concat, not ident
  line-start only (i==0 or prev == "\n")
  skip spaces/tabs after needle
  let start = k
  while is_al (alnum/_ including leading digit): k = k + 1
  let name = str_slice(src, start, k) // ONE slice, not concat
  empty → ERR secret invalid name + process_exit(1)
  c_env_put __sec__+name and __secref__+name
```

Grep inside the function body:

| Pattern | Hits |
|---------|------|
| `name = name + c` | **0** |
| `name = name +` | **0** |
| `out = out +` | **0** |
| `ident = ident +` | **0** |
| `str_slice(src, start, k)` | **1** (L65) |

Classification still uses `char_at` (1-char `OoStr` per visit) and the
70-line `is_al` oracle. Language floor + pre-existing copy, not
quadratic ident accumulate. Domain A already named both.

File-wide: `name = name + c` **absent**. Other `str_slice` is L254
`__sec_sink__` prefix (2.10; not 7.10).

Remaining `+` on this path: needle `"// "+"SECRET:"` and one
`__sec__`/`__secref__` prefix per directive — **O(1) per hit**, not
per ident char.

